  "body": "Closes the bounded register-file hashing scope of #64, stacked on independently accepted PR #63 at `990f36830c5a9854bf8e2cf1fe7fd7d4ccf7f192` ([review](https://github.com/jliu67/OpenRX/pull/63#pullrequestreview-5505712453)). After each of the first seven programs, the new stage hashes the exact native 256-byte R/F/E/A register file and holds its state, tag, controls and 64-byte seed until acknowledged. The eighth program bypasses hashing. The connected tests generate the next program from the actual hardware seed.\n\nThe pinned BSD-2-Clause cyrozap core restarts its chaining value on the second block; preserved native negative tests demonstrate the mismatch. A separate declared derivative corrects continuation while retaining the original arithmetic, schedule and 12 rounds. Independently parameterized 32-byte hashing accepts the caller's post-AES register file. All five selected IP originals, 171 pinned native files and 69 accepted execution inputs remain unchanged.\n\nValidation at `4f095fc147b5bc78de79746a0a172f38e34d6450`: all 18 RTL and 17 mapped modes pass. Both digest sizes use the same 524 native messages, crosschecked against pinned C and Python hashlib. Coverage includes held results, changing inputs, invalid lengths/iterations, reset in both blocks, final bypass, eight native cancellation modes and opposite-version restarts. Four v1/v2 ideal/stalled eight-program \u00d7 four-iteration chains compare full state, native events and all 2 MiB at every program boundary. Their clocks are 111348/185810 (v2) and 70524/121278 (v1), exactly 414 above the accepted software-seed fixture; digest/bridge latency is 56/58 modeled clocks.\n\nActual server Yosys 0.9 mapping covers only the new stages:\n\n| Stage | Generic cells | Flip-flops | Latches |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| hash-64 | 45,891 | 5,156 | 1,024 |\n| hash-32 | 45,635 | 5,156 | 1,024 |\n| seed | 57,378 | 7,755 | 1,024 |\n\nMapped units reproduce the RTL records exactly; the accepted execution backend remains RTL in connected gate tests. [Design](https://github.com/jliu67/OpenRX/blob/4f095fc147b5bc78de79746a0a172f38e34d6450/rtl/hash/README.md), [EXP-011](https://github.com/jliu67/OpenRX/blob/4f095fc147b5bc78de79746a0a172f38e34d6450/experiments/EXP-011-native-regfile-blake2b.md) and [evidence](https://github.com/jliu67/OpenRX/blob/4f095fc147b5bc78de79746a0a172f38e34d6450/docs/validation/regfile-blake2b-20261013/README.md) bind exact inputs, commands, tools, licensed cell models, failures and complete archived outputs. The admitted serial server run used a 2 GiB memory limit, 512 MiB swap limit and a six-CPU quota/affinity under the global compute lock. Source/output archives verify every byte and mode and preserve executable bits.\n\nHosted [run 38457360319](https://github.com/jliu67/OpenRX/actions/runs/38457360319) passed all 18 RTL and 17 mapped modes, and all five checks are green. Complete [artifact 11852734671](https://github.com/jliu67/OpenRX/actions/runs/38457360319/artifacts/11852734671) is verified: 245 uploaded outputs match their manifest, all 246 source bindings and all 35 PASS records match the server, native fixtures/extractions and six licenses are checked, and the exact installed cell model is retained. ZIP SHA256 `f655d9be95a6f0956924d5d6b416688d70c42eb7556f17494c2dd9585f3b6618`. This draft requires new independent review; there is no merge authorization. Initial input hashing, scratchpad AES fill, program AES generation, final scratchpad AES reduction, the real dataset, complete hardware finalization and physical PPA remain external or open. No full 16,384-iteration or whole-core baseline was regenerated.\n\nReproduce in an admitted isolated snapshot with a fresh external output directory:\n\n```sh\npython3 scripts/test_regfile_blake2b.py --output /tmp/openrx-hash-fresh --synthesize\n```\n\n\nBase update: PR #63 was owner-approved and merged as `8f3b9bc3d7f0182d66185abe95310f0bab00274b`. This draft now targets main; its tree is exactly the original accepted base `990f36830c5a9854bf8e2cf1fe7fd7d4ccf7f192` (`e5086cd4f89851f0036743e63fc3aea574fbe957`). Feature head, executed inputs and scientific workload remain unchanged; the existing hosted validation continues without restart. The original provenance and initial publication snapshots remain retained.\n\nHosted mapping uses Yosys 0.33 (git sha1 2584903a060), kept separate from the server Yosys 0.9 counts. hash-64: 41,684 generic cells / 5,154 flops / 1,024 latches; hash-32: 41,172 generic cells / 4,898 flops / 1,024 latches; seed: 44,686 generic cells / 7,753 flops / 1,024 latches. These measurements establish no physical PPA or full-hash throughput. The uploaded ZIP permissions are retained as supplied by the artifact service; the complete server archive separately verifies original byte/modes and executable bits.\n",
